30,2,1,talk,May,,"It seems some old ideas actually worked, specifically late-evening services and contactless payments. However, lane-priority projects have a habit of failing.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"My findings are concerning. Our staffing is depleted, especially for late turns and roadway crews, though we have capacity for lift and escalator maintenance.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Midori,,"Interestingly, mid-city travel takes longer now, but the crowds aren't the main issue. The real time-sink is waiting for connections, not the ticketing process.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"I've found that work in old stations is risky due to unrecorded voids, and there is a lack of agreement between ferry and rail offices.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"We are paying far too much to multiple ticketing contractors, and our technology budget is shrinking while we have a ring-fenced construction balance.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,May,,"@Jonathan, if the technology budget is trimmed, a new fare platform might be tough unless we use that ring-fenced balance.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Midori, if connection times are the problem, we must be careful not to add more complexity to the rosters.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, that's a fair point. We should prioritize a plan that doesn't overstretch the remaining crew.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@May, since lane-priority failed before and old stations are unpredictable, perhaps we should look for the path of least resistance.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"The current ticketing fees are a drain. Consolidating them would save money in the long run, despite the initial cost.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,May,,The late-evening pilot was a success years ago. It might be a safe bet if we can solve the staffing.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,Staffing is exactly the problem. The late-turn pool is thin. Extending night services would be a nightmare for the current crews.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Midori,,"If the mid-city route is slower but not more crowded, maybe a dedicated corridor isn't the answer, but better connection timing is.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Shizue,,The joint operators' disagreement makes an integrated fare system sound like a bureaucratic struggle.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,I agree with Shizue. The lack of data agreement between rail and ferry suggests the Integrated Fare Platform would stall.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,May,,"So, the bus corridor is risky and the fare platform is a bureaucratic mess. That leaves station upgrades or night services.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,Station upgrades seem most viable. We have spare capacity in the lift and escalator maintenance contract.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Midori,,"I agree. If we improve how people move through stations, we might help those connection times I found in the audits.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Shizue,,But the pre-war shells are dangerous and expensive. We must be very careful with the budget there.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,We have a ring-fenced construction balance. Using it for station upgrades avoids the trimmed technology and operating budgets.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,3,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
