55,3,1,talk,May,,I'll vote for Station Access Upgrades. The previous accessibility programme had a decent success rate with rebuilds.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,I concur. It's the only plan that aligns with our current maintenance capacity without breaking the exhausted crews.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Midori,,"I'll support Station Access Upgrades too. It addresses the movement of passengers, which is where the time is lost.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"I am worried about the voids in the shells, but the other options have even greater hurdles. I will vote for C.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,I agree. It utilizes the construction balance and removes the need for the technology budget. I vote for C.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,May,,It seems we are in total agreement.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,Logic dictates this is the most sustainable choice.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Midori,,I'm glad we found a balanced solution.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Shizue,,It is a peaceful conclusion for us all.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,Indeed.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
